Subject: [PATCH] GS GPU renderer: the player's silhouette into his shadow map drawn by the emulated path (TODO 203)

In Amazon the GPU renderer left out the player's whole shadow (a dark band over the ground and the rock wall beside
him, at every scale). The game draws his silhouette into a 128-wide shadow map (FBW 2), softens it, moves its colour
bits into the top byte through a 16-bit view and has the shadow receivers alpha-test that byte. Drawn by the native
pixel path the silhouette came out with alpha 254 where the GS writes 255 (1718 pixels of the map's second half
measured, the emulated path 255 there), which through the shuffle the receivers' test left out. A textured model -
not a sprite, its texture not a buffer - drawn into a buffer at most 128 wide now goes the emulated path; the map's
clear and softening copies and the glow's working buffers of the same width stay native.

Checked against the software renderer (PS2X_GPU_MIRROR=1) on the user's Amazon state: GPU minus software mean 10.1 ->
-0.3 (scale 1) and 0.5 (scale 4), the shadow back. Easter Island unchanged (-0.4). GPU time per frame at scale 8 with
8 samples on a GTX 1080 unchanged within noise (40.7 vs 40.5 ms). PS2X_GPU_NATIVE_SMALL=1: natively, as before.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
index 10f54fb..f21cb80 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
@@ -3000,6 +3000,22 @@ bool GSGpuRenderer::Impl::nativeDraw(const Target &frame, bool usesDepth, Kind d
         return false;
     if (usesDepth && depthKind != kZ32)
         return false;
+    // (TODO 203) A model drawn into a buffer at most 128 pixels wide (FBW 2 or less) with a texture from local memory -
+    // the player's silhouette into his shadow map - through the emulated path: the game reads that buffer back bit by
+    // bit (a 16-bit view's shuffle into the top byte, then an alpha test against it), and drawn natively the
+    // silhouette came out with alpha 254 where the GS writes 255, which the shadow receivers' alpha test then left out:
+    // the whole shadow under the player (Amazon). The buffer's other draws stay native (its clear, its softening
+    // copies, the glow's working buffers of the same width: sprites, or textures from buffers). PS2X_GPU_NATIVE_SMALL=1:
+    // natively, as before.
+    static const bool smallNative = envFlag("PS2X_GPU_NATIVE_SMALL", false);
+    if (!smallNative && std::max<uint32_t>(ctx.frame.fbw, 1u) <= 2u && state.prim.tme && state.prim.type != GS_PRIM_SPRITE)
+    {
+        bool fromBuffer = false;
+        for (const auto &t : targets)
+            fromBuffer = fromBuffer || t->bp == ctx.tex0.tbp0;
+        if (!fromBuffer)
+            return false;
+    }
     if (!fieldPicture && fields && (frame.shadowed || (state.scanmsk & 3u) >= 2u))
         return false;
     if (fieldPicture && (usesDepth || (state.prim.abe && ((ctx.alpha >> 4u) & 3u) == 1u && fpsm == GS_PSM_CT32)))
